# Cloudflare Pages _redirects — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Any specific rewrites or redirects go ABOVE the catch-all so they run first.
# Cloudflare processes rules top-to-bottom and stops at the first match.
#
# (No explicit rewrites at present.)
#
# Catch-all 404 for anything not matching a real static file. Without this
# Cloudflare Pages was serving index.html with a 200 status for unknown
# URLs — a soft-404 that confused users and hurt SEO. The `404` status
# code at the end tells CF Pages to serve /404.html with an actual HTTP
# 404 status, which is the correct semantic response.
/*    /404.html    404
